==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*solh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|salutacioun}}, from {{der|en|fro|salutacion}}, from {{der|en|la|salutatio||a greeting, a wishing health to}}, from {{m|la|saluto||wish one’s health, greet}}, from {{m|la|salus||well-being}}. Compare the Latin greeting {{m|la|salveo|salve|lit=be well}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsæljuˈteɪʃən/|/ˌsæljəˈteɪʃən/}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən}}
* {{hyph|en|sal|u|ta|tion}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# A [[greeting]], [[salute]], or [[address]]; a [[hello]].
# The act of greeting.
#* {{RQ:Critical Pronouncing Dictionary|page=571|passage={{smallcaps|Welcome}}, we²l'ku²m. a.<br> Received with gladneſs, admitted willingly, grateful{{...}}<br>{{smallcaps|Welcome}}, we²l'ku²m. interj.<br> A form of '''ſalutation''' uſed to a new comer.|ppage=1}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Quickening; excitement.

